<P class=3D"topic-title first">NEWS!!!</P>
<P>July 19, 2007</P>
<BLOCKQUOTE>F2PY is now part of <A class=3Dreference=20
  href=3D"http://numpy.scipy.org/">NumPy</A>. All the development and =
maintenance=20
  of F2PY is carried out under NumPy SVN tree. See <A class=3Dreference=20
  href=3D"http://www.scipy.org/F2py">F2PY</A> for more information. If =
you need=20
  F2PY with Numeric or Numarray array support then you must use the F2PY =
version=20
  found below.</BLOCKQUOTE>
<P>January 30, 2005</P>
<BLOCKQUOTE>Latest F2PY release (version 2.45.241_1926). New features:=20
  wrapping unsigned integers, support for <TT class=3D"docutils =
literal"><SPAN=20
  class=3Dpre>.pyf.src</SPAN></TT> template files, callback arguments =
can now be=20
  CObjects, fortran objects, built-in functions. Introduced <TT=20
  class=3D"docutils literal"><SPAN class=3Dpre>intent(aux)</SPAN></TT> =
attribute.=20
  Wrapped objects have <TT class=3D"docutils literal"><SPAN=20
  class=3Dpre>_cpointer</SPAN></TT> attribute holding C pointer to =
wrapped=20
  functions or variables. Many bug fixes and improvements, updated=20
  documentation. <A class=3Dreference=20
  =
href=3D"http://cens.ioc.ee/cgi-bin/cvsweb/python/f2py2e/docs/HISTORY.txt.=
diff?r1=3D1.163&amp;r2=3D1.137&amp;f=3Dh">Differences=20
  with the previous release (version 2.43.239_1831)</A>.</BLOCKQUOTE>
<DL class=3Ddocutils>
  <DT>October 4, 2004=20
  <DD>F2PY bug fix release (version 2.43.239_1831). Better support for =
64-bit=20
  platforms. Introduced <TT class=3D"docutils literal"><SPAN=20
  class=3Dpre>--help-link</SPAN></TT> and <TT class=3D"docutils =
literal"><SPAN=20
  class=3Dpre>--link-&lt;resource&gt;</SPAN></TT> options. Bug fixes. <A =

  class=3Dreference=20
