class=3Dreference=20
href=3D"https://sysbio.ioc.ee/projects/f2py2e/rel-5.x">rel-5.x</A>, if =
you need=20
them.</P>
<P>Development version of F2PY from CVS is available as <A =
class=3Dreference=20
href=3D"http://cens.ioc.ee/cgi-bin/viewcvs.cgi/python/f2py2e/f2py2e.tar.g=
z?tarball=3D1">f2py2e.tar.gz</A>.</P>
<P>Debian Sid users can simply install <TT class=3D"docutils =
literal"><SPAN=20
class=3Dpre>python-f2py</SPAN></TT> package.</P></DIV>
<DIV class=3Dsection>
<H1><A id=3Dinstallation class=3Dtoc-backref=20
href=3D"https://sysbio.ioc.ee/projects/f2py2e/#id42"=20
name=3Dinstallation>Installation</A></H1>
<P>Unpack the source file, change to directrory <TT=20
class=3D"docutils literal"><SPAN class=3Dpre>F2PY-?-???/</SPAN></TT> and =
run (you=20
may need to become a root):</P><PRE class=3Dliteral-block>python =
setup.py install
</PRE>
<P>The F2PY installation installs a Python package <TT=20
class=3D"docutils literal"><SPAN class=3Dpre>f2py2e</SPAN></TT> to your =
Python <TT=20
class=3D"docutils literal"><SPAN class=3Dpre>site-packages</SPAN></TT> =
directory and=20
a script <TT class=3D"docutils literal"><SPAN =
class=3Dpre>f2py</SPAN></TT> to your=20
Python executable path.</P>
<P>See also <A class=3Dreference=20
href=3D"https://sysbio.ioc.ee/projects/f2py2e/FAQ.html#installation">Inst=
allation</A>=20
section in <A class=3Dreference=20
href=3D"https://sysbio.ioc.ee/projects/f2py2e/FAQ.html">F2PY =
FAQ</A>.</P>
<P>Similarly, to install <TT class=3D"docutils literal"><SPAN=20
class=3Dpre>scipy_distutils</SPAN></TT>, unpack its tar-ball and =
run:</P><PRE class=3Dliteral-block>python setup.py install
</PRE></DIV>
<DIV class=3Dsection>
<H1><A id=3Dusage class=3Dtoc-backref=20
href=3D"https://sysbio.ioc.ee/projects/f2py2e/#id43" =
name=3Dusage>Usage</A></H1>
<P>To check if F2PY is installed correctly, run</P><PRE =
class=3Dliteral-block>f2py
</PRE>
<P>without any arguments. This should print out the usage information of =
the <TT=20
class=3D"docutils literal"><SPAN class=3Dpre>f2py</SPAN></TT> =
program.</P>
<P>Next, try out the following three steps:</P>
<OL class=3Darabic>
  <LI>
  <P class=3Dfirst>Create a Fortran file <A class=3Dreference=20
  href=3D"https://sysbio.ioc.ee/projects/f2py2e/hello.f">hello.f</A> =
that=20
  contains:</P><PRE class=3Dliteral-block>C File hello.f
      subroutine foo (a)
      integer a
      print*, "Hello from Fortran!"
      print*, "a=3D",a
      end
</PRE></LI></OL>
<OL class=3D"arabic simple" start=3D2>
  <LI>Run </LI></OL>
<BLOCKQUOTE><PRE class=3Dliteral-block>f2py -c -m hello hello.f
</PRE>
  <P>This will build an extension module <TT class=3D"docutils =
literal"><SPAN=20
  class=3Dpre>hello.so</SPAN></TT> (or <TT class=3D"docutils =
literal"><SPAN=20
  class=3Dpre>hello.sl</SPAN></TT>, or <TT class=3D"docutils =
literal"><SPAN=20
  class=3Dpre>hello.pyd</SPAN></TT>, etc. depending on your platform) =
into the=20
  current directory.</P></BLOCKQUOTE>
<OL class=3Darabic start=3D3>
  <LI>
  <P class=3Dfirst>Now in Python try:</P><PRE =
class=3Dliteral-block>&gt;&gt;&gt; import hello
&gt;&gt;&gt; print hello.__doc__
&gt;&gt;&gt; print hello.foo.__doc__
&gt;&gt;&gt; hello.foo(4)
 Hello from Fortran!
 a=3D 4
&gt;&gt;&gt;
</PRE></LI></OL>
<P>If the above works, then you can try out more thorough <A =
class=3Dreference=20
href=3D"https://sysbio.ioc.ee/projects/f2py2e/FAQ.html#q-how-to-test-if-f=
2py-is-working-correctly">F2PY=20
unit tests</A> and read the <A class=3Dreference=20
href=3D"https://sysbio.ioc.ee/projects/f2py2e/usersguide/index.html">F2PY=
 Users=20
Guide and Reference Manual</A>.</P></DIV>
